{"name":"Fuego","hex":"#ee5533","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[],"entries":[{"title":"Volcán de Fuego","blocks":[{"text":"Volcán de Fuego  or Chi Q'aq' is an active stratovolcano in Guatemala, on the borders of Chimaltenango, Escuintla and Sacatepéquez departments."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/25/In_Antigua_Guatemala-Volcan_de_Fuego_%286849909334%29.jpg/330px-In_Antigua_Guatemala-Volcan_de_Fuego_%286849909334%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Volc%C3%A1n_de_Fuego","wikidata":"Q859376"},{"title":"Tierra del Fuego","blocks":[{"text":"Tierra del Fuego is an archipelago off the southernmost tip of the South American mainland, across the Strait of Magellan."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/62/NASA_Tierra_del_Fuego_image.jpg/330px-NASA_Tierra_del_Fuego_image.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tierra_del_Fuego","wikidata":"Q82601"},{"title":"Fuego (Eleni Foureira song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Fuego\" is a song by Greek singer Eleni Foureira. The song was produced by Alex Papaconstantinou, Didrick and Victory, who also served as co-writers with Anderz Wrethov and Geraldo Sandell. It was released as a single for digital download and streaming on 9 March 2018 in Greece and in various countries on 19 May by A-P, Panik and Sony. Incorporating ethnic and traditional elements, it is an upbeat dance and pop song, with the lyrics addressing female empowerment as well as emancipation and strength."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/e/e0/Fuego_-_Eleni_Foureira.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fuego_(Eleni_Foureira_song)","wikidata":"Q47498866"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/A_glimpse_of_Guatemala_3